# The Wayfinder commit redline is built and tested against.
#
# Wayfinder is consumed read-only and never committed here (validate.sh check
# #6): CI and local dev *materialise* it into vendor/wayfinder via
# scripts/vendor-wayfinder.sh. This file is what makes that materialisation
# reproducible — without it CI tracked a moving branch, so a commit upstream of
# us could turn redline red with nothing changed on our side, and no SHA to
# bisect.
#
# Why a pin file and not a git submodule: a submodule checkout puts *all* of
# Wayfinder's packages under vendor/wayfinder/packages/*, which our pnpm
# workspace glob would absorb — dragging @huggingface/transformers, the
# OpenTelemetry SDK, minio, docx and pdf-parse into redline's install. The
# vendoring script deliberately copies only the one package we consume
# (WAYFINDER_PACKAGES, default: domain).
#
# johntooth/wayfinder is the only Wayfinder redline builds or runs against —
# the same repo services/wayfinder mounts (.gitmodules), and the same branch.
# rbrasier is not a build source here. CI reads both fields literally
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml checks out `repo` @ `ref`), so they are a live
# source, not a label.
#
# The ref tracks the fork's LATEST `main` — not a held-back pin. redline owns
# this fork, so its `main` moves because redline moved it; sitting on an older
# commit is not a choice to consume an older Wayfinder, it is failing to pick up
# work we just did. Move this ref and the services/wayfinder gitlink together in
# the same step; the two drifting apart is what let redline typecheck against a
# domain package the fork had already moved past. validate.sh #15(b) fails when
# they disagree, and it does not skip on a clone with no submodule.
#
# To bump: change ref below, re-run scripts/vendor-wayfinder.sh, then
# `pnpm install && ./validate.sh`. The drift check
# (packages/redline-adapters/src/wayfinder/wayfinder-contract.test.ts) is what
# tells you whether the new commit still satisfies the contract redline reuses.

repo=johntooth/wayfinder
ref=06f0b7621c3cfab1d81986a2a895b213ebab778a
